    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n114003" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χῑλῐέτ-ης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>,
			ὁ, or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χῑλῐετ-ετής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">έος</span>, ὁ<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">,
			ἡ</span>:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>lasting a thousand years,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περίοδος, πορεία,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phdr.</u>
				249a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>R.</u>
				621d
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βίος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>GA</u>
					745a34
				</span></i>
			: fem. acc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ετιν</span>
			v.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				615a
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χειλιέτης ἀγών,</span> celebration of
			the <i>thousandth anniversary</i> of the founding of Rome, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				22.3169.14
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii A. D.)</span>.</div>
